...What had Granny Ichihime said?

The <ruby>guarded<rt>guarded</rt></ruby> school of the Owari Tokugawa. The Kan-ryuu spearpoint, kept hidden inside one domain for two hundred years because it was regarded as the supreme art of spearmanship. How do you seal that with a sword...

What was it again?

&#x27;Countermeasure? Hmm, let me think.&#x27;

&#x27;Can&#x27;t dodge your way out of it. Block it and you only get knocked away.&#x27;

&#x27;Nothing. No way. Absolutely not.&#x27;

Inside my memory, my own voice answered those irresponsible words exactly as it had then.

Inside that memory, the irresponsible old woman shrugged with a mild sneer and went on.

&#x27;A sword can&#x27;t do anything about it. If you still want to win that badly, bring a pistol or something.&#x27;
